.TH "KZ-SETUP.SH" "5" "4.2.1" "kz" "File format"
.ad l

.SH NAME
kz-setup.sh - settings file for use with kz setup

.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY kz-setup.sh
.YS

.SH DESCRIPTION
This file contains commands to process as an settings file with kz setup.
.br
Commands containing personal information, such as a username, are included in
an GPG-encrypted settings file, kz-setup.sh.gpg.
.sp
The settings file contains contains so-called \fBapp-\fR and \
\fBcommand record\fRs.
.sp
The \fBapp record\fR indicates for which app and which computer the commands
should be executed and provides a description of the app.
.br
These records are followed by one or more records with commands, the
\fBcommand record\fRs.
.sp
See \fBTable 1\fR for which \fBtypes\fR records there are and how these records
are processed.
.sp
See \fBTable 2\fR for an \fBexample\fR of these records in file
kz-setup.sh.
.br
More examples can be seen through the \fBkz setup --browse\fR and
\fBkz setup --cat\fR commands.
.LP
.B Table 1. Record types and their processing
.TS
allbox tab(^);
lbx lbx
l l.
Record^Description
# Setup: APP | HOST... | DESCRIPTION^Set up the app (\fBapp-record\fR), will b\
e processed.
# Comment^Comment line (none, one or more), will be skipped.
Command^Setup command (one or more \fBcommand record\fRs), will be executed.
^Empty line (none, one or more), will be skipped.
# Reset: APP | HOST... | DESCRIPTION^Reset the app (\fBapp-record\fR for optio\
n \fB-r\fR, \fB--reset\fR), will be processed.
Command^Reset command (one or more \fBcommand record\fRs), will be executed.
.TE
.LP
.B Table 2. Example of records and their processing
.TS
box tab(^);
lb | lbx
- | -
l | l.
Record^Description
# Setup: calibre | * | Powerful and easy to use e-book manager^Set up calibre \
on every computer, see [1].
kz-desktop --addbef=calibre-gui^Setup command for calibre.
^
# Reset: calibre | * | Powerful and easy to use e-book manager^Reset calibre o\
n every computer, see [1].
kz-desktop --delete=calibre-gui^Reset command for calibre.
^
^
# Setup: vscode | pc06 pc07 | Code editing. Redefined^Set up vscode on pc06 an\
d pc07, see [2].
# kz-desktop --addaft=code^Setup command for vscode.
^
# Reset: vscode | pc06 pc07 | Code editing. Redefined^Reset vscode on pc06 and\
 pc07, see [2].
kz-desktop --delete=code^Reset command for vscode.
.TE
.sp
[1]
.br
The line with '*' as HOST causes the associated commands to run on all
computers.
.sp
A line with 'pc01' as HOST ensures that the associated commands are executed
only on pc01 by default.
.br
A line with 'pc01 pc02' as HOST ensures that the associated commands are
executed only on pc01 and pc02 by default.
.br
A line with '#none' as HOST ensures that the associated commands are not
executed by default (NOTE: '#none' is not a valid computername and will
therefore never be selected by default).
.sp
[2]
.br
An app can still be set up on another computer with the command 'kz setup
APP', e.g. 'kz setup vscode'. In that case, the content of HOST is ignored.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkz-setup\fR(1),
\fBkz-setup.sh.gpg\fR(5)
